  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "The shooting snake – curve in and shoot",
  "description": "The players stand in a line in one corner, and a pile of pucks lies in the other corner at the same end. The first player skates with the puck in a curve in towards goal and shoots. Then they skate to the other corner, take a new puck and do the same in the other direction. The next in line starts once the one ahead has shot.\n\nShooting without opposition but with a bit of pressure. Choose the shot for each round: wrist shot, snap shot or backhand. Smart, accurate shots usually score more than hard ones. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "How do you aim? Look at the goal, not the puck, just before you shoot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "How hard do you need to shoot? Placement beats power."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Shoot on the move – do not stop before the shot."
    }
  ],
